      "answer": "Healthcare workers should perform hand hygiene at five moments: before touching a patient, before a clean or aseptic procedure, after body fluid exposure risk, after touching a patient, and after touching patient surroundings. They should also clean hands before donning gloves and again after removing gloves.",
