      "answer": "Staff may return to work 5 days after symptom onset if they have been fever-free for at least 24 hours without fever-reducing medication and symptoms are improving, counting the day symptoms start as day 0. They must wear a well-fitting mask in all patient care areas through day 10 after symptom onset. Staff who work with severely immunocompromised patients should have a negative test result on day 5 or later before returning, or remain off work until day 10.",
